{
	title: 'Prompt-file change notices, scoped to the project',
	spec: "When a file the system prompt reads changes, the user sees a notice popup (the qm stack), never a scrollback line, so scrollback does not fill with them. SYSTEM.md and the files it includes (they bust the prompt cache the same way) go to every client watching a tab. An AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md change goes only to clients whose shown tab it applies to: the file sits in a directory from that tab cwd up to its Git root (systemPrompt.candidates), so a project AGENTS.md shows only in tabs inside that project. The notice names the file, says changed, created or deleted, and gives its path; each save is its own notice, stacked, so two saves show two. Opening a tab or starting the host announces nothing: a file is compared only with what the host saw before. Only the host checks (src/host/prompt-files.ts), by polling, the same on every platform: tabs a client shows every second, tabs a turn runs in every half second, other tabs never. Idle costs little: a pass stats each file (mtime, size, inode) and reads only files whose stat changed; it rebuilds a tab's prompt to list its files only when the prompt input (session settings, interactive flag, Git root candidates, trust, plugin hooks) changed or one of its files did. A same-size write within one mtime tick goes unseen. Test: a change reaches the tabs it applies to and no others; SYSTEM.md reaches all.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Polls (readFileSync per pass) instead of fs.watch: the watched set follows which tab each client shows and its cwd, and editors save by rename; comparing contents also ignores touches. Uses the update kind (neutral color) with what = changed/created/deleted and key prompt-file:<path>; session is the receiving client's shown tab, so a web tap stays put. Not recorded in notice history: entries need a session and these are not about one. Files SYSTEM.md includes are not watched.",
		'Watched set per shown tab = systemPrompt.inspect sources (SYSTEM.md, its includes, present AGENTS.md) plus every AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md candidate, so creation is seen too; a missing optional @? include is not. Every detection and delivery goes to diag.log as "prompt files: ...". An edit made before the host starts is its baseline and is never announced: the first report of "nothing happens" was a SYSTEM.md saved before the restart that loaded this code.',
		'Latency: a terminal without focus is not "visible", so prompt-file notices waited for focus. host.ts records `shown` (the tab a client shows, focused or not) and prompt-files routes by it; fs.watch on the watched files\' directories (renames by editors included) triggers a check within 30 ms, the 1 s poll remains for tab and cwd changes.',
		'User correction: repeated saves must stack, not replace one per-path notice. Keys carry a per-change counter.',
		'Idle CPU (ADEMark A6, 2026-11-13): the 1 s poll rebuilt every shown tab prompt (systemPrompt.inspect, prompt-lang render, skills readdir, pages.findLast for interactive) just to list its files: about half of an idle host CPU profile, 3.8 ms per pass. Now cached per tab under a key of promptCache.input (now zeroed), candidates and trust; interactive is reread only when the history size (pages.marks) grows. fs.watch on directories was removed: polling is simpler and identical on macOS and Linux, and it also covers network mounts. This supersedes the fs.watch latency note. Measured idle host+client 20-80 s: 1.25 % of a core before, 0.87-0.97 % after; the rest is mostly the client cursor blink (pulse) and projectContext.allowed realpathSync. Bug fixed on the way: a turn in a tab nobody shows got no trail record (task ar) for its own AGENTS.md edit until another tab noticed a change; invariant: every tab a turn runs in is polled.'
	],
	needs: ['qm', '29']
